  "id": "c4326ca2-e2eb-5dcc-9f7c-3dc31ce1df70",
  "slug": "hawaiian-roll-honey-buns-recipe-11943525",
  "name": "Hawaiian Roll Honey Buns",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "These Hawaiian roll honey buns are unapologetically sweet and soft in the best way. The rolls are pillowy, with a subtly crisp exterior coated in a glossy, sweet glaze. The filling is rich, sweet, warm, and\u2014thanks to the honey\u2014not just straight-up sweet, but also some complexity. It\u2019s tough to put these down.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees F (180 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Stir together light brown sugar, 1/3 cup butter, 2 tablespoons honey, and 1 1/2 teaspoons cinnamon in a bowl. Using a long serrated knife, split the entire loaf of rolls horizontally. Do not separate into individual rolls. Spread butter mixture evenly over cut-side of bottom rolls, then cover with top rolls. Carefully transfer rolls to a small, parchment paper-lined baking sheet."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Melt 1 tablespoon butter in a small saucepan over medium heat, then brush evenly over tops of rolls; do not wash saucepan."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Bake rolls in the preheated oven until golden and warmed through, 8 to 10 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Meanwhile, cook remaining 1 tablespoon butter, 1 tablespoon honey, and 1/2 teaspoon cinnamon in reserved saucepan over medium heat, stirring constantly, until melted and smooth, about 1 minute. Remove from heat and stir in powdered sugar, water, vanilla, and salt. Brush mixture evenly over warm rolls, and serve immediately. Recipe developed by Craig Ruff"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 12,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 10,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 10,
